## Modifications

All changes made in this fork relative to the fork point above are
Copyright (c) 2026 koro and are likewise licensed under `AGPL-3.0-only`, as
required by the upstream license. Section 5(a) of the AGPL asks modified files
to carry prominent notices stating that they were changed and the date. Because
this repository is entirely derived from Honcho, every modified or added file is
listed below with its last-modification date, which records the changes for the
whole repository in one place.

Functional summary of the changes:

- **Identity and display names** — observe peers as `display name (stable id)`
  built from QQ group cards stored in `session_peers`, with a per-session
  roster, name history (曾用名), duplicate-name disambiguation, roster staleness
  bounds, first-description sampling over full history, and a contradiction
  write path in the deriver.
- **Session profiles and representation** — session-level venue description plus
  zero-LLM member statistics, long-term impression compression (plan B of
  §18/§19), "today is …" and fixed-facts sections, compact timestamp rendering
  with cross-session provenance.
- **Dreamer** — per-session dream windows, off-peak (谷时) scheduling with
  jitter, injection of "now" into dreamer prompts, profile refresh tests.
- **Deriver** — runner/consumer split, contradiction write path, prompt updates.
- **Knowledge Entries API (new)** — workspace-scoped explicit knowledge storage
  with a pgvector HNSW index, idempotent create, semantic query, and route-level
  tests (`POST/GET/PATCH/DELETE /v3/workspaces/{workspace_id}/knowledge`).
- **Operations** — single-process Windows-compatible entry point (`start.ps1`),
  explicit `SelectorEventLoop`, telemetry/metrics adjustments, local
  configuration template (`.env.template`).
- **Privacy** — real chat identifiers that had been used as examples were
  replaced with placeholder values (`123456789012`) in this fork's history and
  source files.
- Removed an internal development task list (`foxbot-dream-sweep-task.md`) that
  never existed upstream.

